    "values": [
      {
        "value": "1-9",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "In 1989, fifty speakers were reported from Latvia and about the same number in parts of the Russian Federation, but these figures were clearly inflated. There is possibly only one speaker with full native competence, which makes the language nearly extinct. At the same time, there are several younger descendants of Livonian speakers who have learnt Livonian as second language and cultivate it actively."
      },
      {
        "value": "10-99",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
